                <pb facs="0688" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg574"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">662.6331/72½: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-03-26T18:00:00-05:00">March 26, 1931—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>13. In a discreet manner you are to inquire whether or not, upon the
                    establishment of the Belgo-Luxemburg Economic Union in 1921, any other
                    Government, in view of an unconditional most-favored-nation clause in an
                    existing treaty with either Belgium or Luxemburg, sought to claim the advantages
                    of the union. What success attended such representation? Please report as soon
                    as possible.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
